okay first we have to learn some new registers
External Interrupt Control Register A(EICRA) is the one we use for the RISING CHANGE and FALLING
cuz unlike PCINT INT has these features out of the box
ISC1x and ISC0x are the macros to change the helper bits macros in EICRA
here is which combi does what:
ISCx0     ISCx1    MODE     WHAZ IT DOES
   0         0      LOW      fires the hole time as long as pin is LOW
   0         1      FALLING  fires if it goes from HIGH to LOW (5v -> 0v) 
   1         0      CHANGE   fires if it changes regardless of HIGH to LOW or LOW to HIGH
   1         1      RISING   fires if it goes from LOW to HIGH (0v -> 5v)

External Interrupt Mask Register (EIMSK) is the same thing as PCMASK but instead of 3 there is only 1
and bit 0(INT0) is pin2 and bit 1(INT1) is pin3 the main difrence is that we dont activate a group but an
direct pin

